      ],
      "text": "14.5 Post-ROSC Coronary Angiography"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If STEMI or new LBBB is identified on post-ROSC 12-lead ECG, emergent coronary angiography & PCI should be performed IMMEDIATELY, regardless of neuro status or coma depth. In pts w/o ST elevation, timing of angiography is guided by clinical suspicion for coronary cause, hemodynamic stability, & institutional protocols - immediate routine catheterization in the absence of STEMI is not required."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
